  "configuration_id": "config_045",
  "reason": "We currently only have two image-only, singleprofile baselines (ResNet50: 0.208, ViT-L: 0.227), which establish that image alone yields modest performance and that ViT-L is the stronger image encoder. The most critical unresolved question is whether the RNA modality carries any predictive signal at all, since no RNA-only or multimodal result exists yet. config_045 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is the cleanest parallel to our existing image-only singleprofile baselines: it isolates the RNA modality with the same profile setting and uses scgpt, the most expressive RNA encoder that appears in the multimodal configurations. This single experiment tells us (a) whether RNA has usable signal, (b) how it compares in magnitude to the image-only baselines, and (c) whether investing further experiments in multimodal fusion is warranted. It changes only the modality relative to our completed baselines, making the comparison direct and interpretable under a tight budget."
}

